  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 140 PM CDT MON SEP 14 2026\n\nPersistent upper-level ridging will remain the weather story for\nthis forecast, as the apex of the ridge is currently establishing\nitself over Tennessee. This ridge will very quickly \"switch off\"\nrain chances for the week, with the highest probabilities in the\nafternoon not even reaching 10% through Friday. Under this high\npressure, afternoon high temperatures will quickly stabilize in\nthe low to upper-90s, remaining here until next weekend as well.\nWhile afternoon temperatures will be hot, dew point values will\nbe lower in this drier airmass. In turn, heat index values will\nmostly range between 101-103, keeping us below any type of heat\ncritical thresholds.\n\nBy this weekend, it appears as if the upper-level pattern begins\nto shift, as a low pressure works its way around the ridge. This\nlow will work into the Gulf via the Atlantic, continuing to work\nwest over the next few days. While confidence in the exact\nplacement and movement of the disturbance is low, anything that\ndoes work into the Gulf should suppress the ridge and increase\nrain chances through the weekend.\n\n/44/",
